    "problem_statement": "Retry logic broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe retry mechanism appears to be completely broken. Functions that should retry multiple times are only executing once, and the retry loop seems to exit prematurely without respecting stop conditions or wait times.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tenacity\n\n@tenacity.retry(stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(3))\ndef failing_function():\n    print(\"Attempt made\")\n    raise Exception(\"This should retry\")\n\ntry:\n    failing_function()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Final exception: {e}\")\n```\n\nExpected: Should print \"Attempt made\" 3 times before raising the final exception.\nActual: Only prints \"Attempt made\" once.\n\nAlso reproducible with context manager:\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import Retrying\n\nattempts = 0\nfor attempt in Retrying(stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(3)):\n    with attempt:\n        attempts += 1\n        print(f\"Attempt {attempts}\")\n        if attempts < 3:\n            raise Exception(\"Retry me!\")\n\nprint(f\"Total attempts: {attempts}\")\n```\n\nExpected: Should make 3 attempts and print \"Total attempts: 3\"\nActual: Only makes 1 attempt and prints \"Total attempts: 1\"\n\nThe retry mechanism seems to be terminating after the first attempt regardless of the configured stop conditions."
